,33390] and 1 in (36751,36990]; **zero events after 36990** (step_08, step_10, step_11).\n- Therefore every interaction touching 1860 in the window happens *before* 1006's first interaction \u2014 no time-respecting sequence out of 1006 can ever reach 1860, regardless of the 600-unit gap constraint.\n- Confounder controls: a static (time-ignoring) connection does exist \u2014 1006's 2-hop shell is tiny (1075, 1532, 1028, 1036, 1643; step_03), but at 4 hops it merges into the hub 274, which statically links to 1860 (step_05, step_06). That hub is high-volume (70 events, 66 partners; step_13), which could create a spurious \"connected\" impression, yet 274\u21921860 has no events after 37471 (step_12). So the apparent connectivity is driven by hub popularity and order-free reachability, not by any valid temporal chain.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9c9c8a9f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [32431, 42031],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"All interactions involving 1860 in the window occur at or before ~36990, while 1006's earliest interaction occurs after ~37470. Since influence must flow forward in time (with gaps <= 600), no time-respecting path from 1006 to 1860 can exist. The only reason the pair looks connected is the order-free reachability through the very high-degree hub 274 (70 events, 66 partners), which has no 274->1860 event after 1006 becomes active. Hence the cascade is absent.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 51383, "total_output_tokens": 4433, "total_tokens": 55816, "total_latency_ms": 66068, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}